#
# Provides the HSV struct representing a color in the Hue-Saturation-Value
# color space. HSV is a cylindrical representation where hue is an angle on
# the color wheel (0-360 degrees), saturation measures the purity of the color
# (0.0-1.0), and value measures the brightness from black (0.0) to the most
# vivid color (1.0). HSV is commonly used in color pickers because it maps
# intuitively to how humans perceive color choices.
#
# This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify
# it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by
# the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or
